The shuffled dataset was then randomly divided into two subsets: 80% for training (Data-train) and 20% for validation (Data-val). Because the calibration dataset was collected using a pure N2 carrier gas, additional tests were conducted to assess model robustness under more realistic conditions. Two separate test datasets were created for this purpose. The first test set (Data-test1) corresponds to indoor measurements using a pump to deliver CH4 calibration gas, while the second test set (Data-test2) was collected outdoors under stable environmental conditions using portable CH4 calibration gas. In all experiments, the reference analyzer provided the ground-truth CH4 concentration values.
