exploration and feature-combination screening, we applied a selection criterion requiring each candidate to achieve R2 > 0.8 on both Data-Val and Data-Test1. Models satisfying this threshold were then ranked by stability and accuracy, yielding six top-performing configurations summarized in Table 1. To further verify robustness under varying environmental conditions (e.g., outdoor variability and potential covariate shift), we subsequently evaluated the shortlisted models on Data-Test2 as an out-of-distribution (OOD) test set. This additional probe is designed to confirm whether gains observed on Data-Val and Data-Test1 translate to stronger generalization beyond the training regime.
